WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:11.511
A dream vacation to

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:12.612
The Bahamas

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:14.080
became a living nightmare

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:15.115
for cruise passengers

00:00:15.115 --> 00:00:16.649
after severe weather

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:19.085
violently rocked the carnival sunshine.

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:21.087
The ship was returning to South Carolina

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:22.922
over the weekend when it hit rough seas

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:24.224
rough, putting it mildly,

00:00:24.224 --> 00:00:25.025
leaving passengers

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:26.192
frightened, wondering

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:28.628
if they would make it back home.

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:29.195
This, of course,

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:30.530
according to one of our next guests,

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:31.131
Bill Hassler,

00:00:31.131 --> 00:00:33.900
who was there for all of the fun.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.702
Not so sure it was fun.

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:37.737
Let's show you this video that he shot.

00:00:37.771 --> 00:00:39.305
You can see all sorts of debris

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:40.940
being tossed around this ship.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:41.674
Also, water

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:43.877
rushing into hallways and rooms.

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:46.112
Carnival said this in a statement.

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:47.447
Quote, Carnival sunshine

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:49.315
return to Charleston was impacted

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:50.216
by the weather

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:51.851
and rough seas on Saturday.

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:53.219
The weather's prolonged impact

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:54.587
on the Charleston area, delayed

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:56.523
the ship's arrival on Sunday.

00:00:56.523 --> 00:00:57.290
And as a result,

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:59.192
the next Voyages embarkation

00:00:59.192 --> 00:00:59.993
was also delayed.

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:00.994
We appreciate the patience

00:01:00.994 --> 00:01:02.262
and understanding of all our guests.

00:01:02.262 --> 00:01:03.063
Carnival Sunshine

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:04.931
is now sailing on its next

00:01:04.931 --> 00:01:06.066
cruise will house

00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:08.034
or was on that ship and joins us now.

00:01:08.034 --> 00:01:09.335
Good morning for now.

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:11.371
I told you, I grew up going on cruises.

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:12.472
Never,

00:01:12.472 --> 00:01:15.175
never did I see something like this.

00:01:15.475 --> 00:01:17.710
What was it like to live through?

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:19.312
Actually, I'm surprised I'm still alive.

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:21.714
Really? Yeah, it was at that. It's

00:01:22.849 --> 00:01:23.917
I've seen the looks on

00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:25.752
people's face when

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:27.720
I was a crane up here in New York City

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:29.255
and I was running a locomotive

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:30.223
for the sand hugs

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:31.324
and I flipped the train over

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:33.626
and saw the 650 feet on the roof.

00:01:33.626 --> 00:01:35.628
And when I climbed out of that train,

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:37.230
the look of fear and death,

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:38.298
they thought it was like

00:01:38.298 --> 00:01:40.266
I seen ghosts, like they seen ghosts.

00:01:40.266 --> 00:01:42.936
And when I got off the ship at six, 7:00

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:44.571
Saturday evening,

00:01:44.571 --> 00:01:45.572
when I was supposed to dock

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:47.207
at eight in the morning,

00:01:47.474 --> 00:01:49.075
the look of that looked at

00:01:49.075 --> 00:01:51.377
I seen on these faces years ago

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:51.811
was the same

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:53.513
look I seen on all these people

00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:54.180
coming off the ship.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.349
Like they were just white waves, ghosts.

00:01:56.616 --> 00:01:57.584
You said at one point

00:01:57.584 --> 00:01:59.686
it seemed like Carnival was playing God

00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:00.420
with your life.

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:00.987
Yeah, exactly.

00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:01.354
I mean,

00:02:01.354 --> 00:02:04.290
why would you sail into this storm

00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:06.926
with 80 mile an hour plus winds

00:02:07.427 --> 00:02:09.062
I mean, who does that?

00:02:09.129 --> 00:02:10.396
I mean, I was a crane operator

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:12.699
and everybody that worked around me

00:02:12.699 --> 00:02:14.701
around a crane or any equipment I was on,

00:02:15.068 --> 00:02:16.669
their lives were in my hands.

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:18.104
So when the winds were bad

00:02:18.104 --> 00:02:19.772
or the weather was bad,

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:21.040
we'd shut the job down

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:23.343
and not work for safety.

00:02:23.343 --> 00:02:25.278
What were they thinking?

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:25.712
Well,

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:27.313
what do you think they should have done?

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:28.448
I think they should have stayed down

00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:30.083
in port in the Bahamas,

00:02:30.083 --> 00:02:31.651
waited a day for the storm

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:33.653
to subside a little bit and then go

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:35.388
or when they got into a storm,

00:02:35.388 --> 00:02:36.422
why didn't they go further out

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:37.624
into the ocean

00:02:37.624 --> 00:02:38.925
to get to the other side of it,

00:02:38.925 --> 00:02:40.326
you know, the backside.

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:42.962
How how accessible in the statement,

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:44.097
Poppy, just shared, they

00:02:44.097 --> 00:02:45.064
thank you for your patience

00:02:45.064 --> 00:02:46.499
and your understand

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:48.001
How much communication was

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:49.169
there as all of this was happening?

00:02:49.169 --> 00:02:49.802
Was there information

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:50.570
on the loudspeakers?

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:52.505
Were you told to go into certain areas?

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:53.907
No. Very little.

00:02:53.907 --> 00:02:55.141
I don't even think the crew knew

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:56.176
what they were doing.

00:02:56.176 --> 00:02:57.343
I don't think they were trained

00:02:57.343 --> 00:02:59.879
enough for a situation like that.

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:01.381
They were actually at one point

00:03:01.381 --> 00:03:03.883
scavenging to get the life boats ready

00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:06.186
to throw us out into

00:03:06.186 --> 00:03:09.656
the sea with 40 plus foot waves.

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:11.291
I don't even know how you would

00:03:11.291 --> 00:03:12.325
even get in the lifeboat

00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:13.359
if that thing went down.

00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:14.794
We were all dead.

00:03:15.128 --> 00:03:17.063
Wow. Yeah.

00:03:17.297 --> 00:03:18.598
At one point,

00:03:18.598 --> 00:03:19.766
a wave hit my window

00:03:19.766 --> 00:03:20.600
and broke my window

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:21.901
and water was coming in.

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:22.769
Coming into the boat.

00:03:22.769 --> 00:03:24.270
Into your state? Yes.

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:26.039
What did you do at that point?

00:03:26.039 --> 00:03:27.373
I put on my life preserver.

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:28.274
You did? Yeah.

00:03:28.274 --> 00:03:30.243
I actually fell asleep at one point

00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:30.743
for a little while

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:32.645
with my life preserver on.

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:35.048
You heard us read Carnival Statement

00:03:35.615 --> 00:03:38.518
I wonder if you want something else

00:03:38.518 --> 00:03:39.252
from them.

00:03:39.252 --> 00:03:39.619
I mean, it

00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:41.221
sounds like you're very concerned

00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:42.855
that preparations weren't made

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:44.624
and safety wasn't prioritized.

00:03:44.624 --> 00:03:45.925
They shouldn't went through a storm,

00:03:45.925 --> 00:03:47.594
and they need to be held accountable.

00:03:47.594 --> 00:03:48.661
What does that look like to you?

00:03:49.829 --> 00:03:51.731
Is it meaning as far as what?

00:03:51.731 --> 00:03:52.932
Well, just not in terms of

00:03:52.932 --> 00:03:55.101
just you being compensated for that.

00:03:55.368 --> 00:03:57.103
Do you fear that could happen again?

00:03:57.103 --> 00:03:58.304
Oh, yeah. Listen.

00:03:58.304 --> 00:04:00.473
It was like a coin toss for them,

00:04:00.473 --> 00:04:02.208
and they got lucky.

00:04:02.208 --> 00:04:03.009
Maybe the next time

00:04:03.009 --> 00:04:04.744
they won't be as lucky.

00:04:05.011 --> 00:04:07.614
You know, what do you think should then?

00:04:07.647 --> 00:04:08.815
You know, just to follow up on Poppy's

00:04:08.815 --> 00:04:09.849
point there, what should change?

00:04:09.849 --> 00:04:10.717
What do you want to see?

00:04:10.717 --> 00:04:11.918
There's got to be different laws

00:04:11.918 --> 00:04:13.519
about heading into storms,

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:14.787
especially when you're not in one.

00:04:14.787 --> 00:04:16.923
How do you sell out of sun into a storm

00:04:16.923 --> 00:04:17.557
like that?

00:04:17.557 --> 00:04:18.925
It made no sense.

00:04:18.925 --> 00:04:19.459
Yeah.

00:04:20.159 --> 00:04:21.527
We're glad you're okay.

00:04:21.527 --> 00:04:22.762
And I'm sure it's traumatizing

00:04:22.762 --> 00:04:24.464
and it's probably all just starting to,

00:04:24.464 --> 00:04:25.632
like, soak in, right?

00:04:25.632 --> 00:04:27.634
I got home Sunday night.

00:04:27.634 --> 00:04:29.335
I had to crack open a beer

00:04:29.335 --> 00:04:30.203
and think about it.

00:04:30.203 --> 00:04:31.871
And I started shaking really?

00:04:31.871 --> 00:04:34.407
Because it just said it like that.

00:04:34.474 --> 00:04:34.741
Like,

00:04:34.741 --> 00:04:36.109
I couldn't even believe I'm still here.

00:04:36.109 --> 00:04:36.776
Like,

00:04:36.943 --> 00:04:39.145
you know, when they say kiss the ground,

00:04:39.145 --> 00:04:40.747
they stick around. Yeah.

00:04:40.747 --> 00:04:41.581
And you're staying on dry

00:04:41.581 --> 00:04:43.549
land for a while. Yeah.

00:04:43.549 --> 00:04:45.451
Staying away from the ocean.

00:04:45.451 --> 00:04:46.753
We're so glad you're okay.

00:04:46.753 --> 00:04:48.087
Thank you very much.

